    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Sleep Apnea Dentist in Tracy CA | Dr Dante Gonzales Orthodontics"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Many people don’t realise how common sleep apnea is until they experience constant tiredness or loud snoring that wakes everyone. At Dr Dante Gonzales Orthodontics, our sleep apnea treatment Tracy CA program is designed to help patients breathe properly through the night and improve overall health. It’s a quiet problem that can cause more than poor sleep. Sometimes it leads to high blood pressure, stroke, or even a heart attack if left untreated."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "When a person with sleep apnea sleeps, the throat muscles relax too much. The soft tissue in the throat collapses, blocking the airway for a few seconds at a time. The brain then forces the body to wake and start breathing again. This cycle may repeat dozens to a hundred of times per night. This leads to very little real sleep."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Schedule Your Sleep Apnea Consultation",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "tracy-ca-orthodontic-office-contact.php",
          "text": "Schedule Your Sleep Apnea Consultation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Common Causes and How We Determine Treatment"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "During your first visit, we review your symptoms and take X-rays or airway scans to determine how your jaw and mouth behave while you sleep. Sometimes jaw forward movement improves the airway naturally. For others, excess soft tissue or weak throat muscles need targeted correction. Every case is different, and we make sure to tailor the care. That’s how we see it anyway."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Our treatment options vary based on your health and comfort. For some, a custom oral appliance keeps the jaw forward slightly, opening the airway and allowing smooth breathing all night. Others combine orthodontic adjustments with weight loss or CPAP therapy for full recovery. It’s about what works for your body."
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "assets/brand/logo-mark.png",
      "alt": "Logo",
      "title": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Want to know if you’re a candidate for braces or Invisalign?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Take Our 30-Second Quiz Now To Find Out!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Take Quiz Now!",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "invisalign-quiz.php",
          "text": "Take Quiz Now!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "How Sleep Apnea Affects Overall Health"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Untreated apnea affects every part of the human body. Low oxygen levels make the brain work harder. Over time, it can cause fatigue, irritability, and poor focus. The lack of deep sleep means the body never rests completely. Even throat dryness and headaches appear frequently."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Patients often describe waking suddenly, feeling like they are choking or gasping. That’s the brain trying to restart breathing. Over months, this stress increases the risk of heart attack or stroke. It also affects metabolism, making weight loss harder. It’s not just snoring, it’s your body signalling distress."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Book an Appointment at Our Tracy Office",
      "links": [
