      "type": "h2",
      "text": "How We Treat Sleep Apnea at Our Tracy Office"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "We start by verifying the condition through proper review of your medical and dental records. Once verification is successful waiting, our orthodontic team prepares a custom treatment plan. For many, the oral appliance is enough, it holds the jaw forward, keeps the throat muscles active, and lets air flow freely."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Each plan is made after a careful review, never rushed. Our services focus on balance, comfort, effectiveness, and safety. Sometimes simple adjustments make a world of difference."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Start Your Sleep Apnea Treatment Today",
      "links": [
        {
          "href": "tracy-ca-orthodontic-office-contact.php",
          "text": "Start Your Sleep Apnea Treatment Today"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "What to Expect During Treatment"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The process feels natural after the first few nights. Some patients say they sleep through the night for the first time in years. You may notice better energy, fewer headaches, and calmer mornings. We schedule regular appointments to track progress, making small changes if required."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The treatment is comfortable and fits easily into a normal bedtime routine. You wear the oral appliance, close your mouth, and breathe freely. The airway stays open, and the brain doesn’t need to panic for oxygen. That’s how proper care should feel, steady, peaceful, and simple"
    },
    {
      "type": "img",
      "src": "assets/locations/tracy/sleep-apnea-tracy-02.jpg",
      "alt": "Thumb",
      "title": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Book Your Sleep Apnea Appointment in Tracy CA Today"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If you’ve noticed loud snoring, gasping during sleep, or constant tiredness, it’s time to act. A quick appointment can change your nights entirely. At our Tracy office, we’re trained in treating airway-related disorders and helping you get consistent, healthy sleep again."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Our approach is designed to work with your body, not against it. Whether it’s a cpap device, oral appliance, or other supportive treatment options, we’ll guide you through safely. And yes, small improvements lead to big results. Feels worth it when mornings start fresh."
    },
