    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. What causes sleep apnea? It happens when throat muscles and soft tissue block the airway for a few seconds during sleep. This interrupts breathing and lowers oxygen levels. 2. How does Dr Dante Gonzales treat sleep apnea? We use oral appliances that keep the jaw forward to open the airway and improve nighttime breathing. Other treatment options are reviewed if needed. 3. Can untreated sleep apnea cause other health issues? Yes. It may lead to high blood pressure, heart attack, stroke, and daytime irritability. Proper treatment can restore healthy sleep and energy. 4. Is sleep apnea treatment painful or uncomfortable? Not at all. Most patients find our treatments gentle and easy to adapt to. The oral appliance fits comfortably and doesn’t interfere with regular sleep. Within a few nights, it often feels completely natural. 5. How soon can I expect results from treatment? Many patients notice better sleep and more energy within the first few weeks. The exact timeline depends on your condition, but consistent use of the appliance or other recommended therapies leads to steady, lasting improvement."
    }
